# ── WHO CHECKS THIS FILE ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Three things read the EFFECT of these rules, so the file and its checkers cannot drift apart
# silently. Change a rule here and one of them goes red:
#
#   1. scripts/harness/guards/commit-hygiene.cjs, the gitignore-gap probe (SHOULD_BE_IGNORED). An
#      UNTRACKED file that git is not ignoring and that matches one of these classes is a BLOCK:
#        dependency tree   node_modules/
#        build output      dist/ build/ out/ coverage/ .next/ .turbo/ .vite/
#        transient file    *.log *.tmp *.temp *.bak *.orig *.rej *.swp *.pid
#        local database    *.db *.sqlite *.sqlite3 *.db-wal *.db-shm *.db-journal
#        OS junk           .DS_Store Thumbs.db desktop.ini
#        compiler cache    *.tsbuildinfo
#        editor backup     *~
#      Every class has a rule below. Add a class there and it needs a rule here, or the first
#      such file anyone creates blocks their commit.
#   2. scripts/harness/common.json `ignore.mustIgnore` / `ignore.mustTrack`, probed by
#      branch-sync.js with `git check-ignore --no-index`: the run output, the local settings, the
#      hygiene waiver, node_modules and a guarded secret file must come out ignored; the config,
#      the shared settings, the agents, the skills and the two committed figure files must not.
#   3. `node bin/harness.js doctor`, which probes the same paths plus one per pattern in
#      `env.guarded` (harness.config.json).
#
# gitignore takes the LAST matching pattern, and it will not re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded. So a negation goes below the rule it overrides, and a directory you
# intend to carve an exception out of is excluded by its contents (`dir/*`), never as `dir/`.

# ── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
.obsidian/

# ── Node ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The harness has ZERO dependencies and no install step, so nothing here should ever exist in
# this repo. These are guards for the day a tool drops one in: a node_modules/ in a repo whose
# CI never installs is a tree only one machine has.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Transient files, local databases, caches, build output ────────
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.pid
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.tsbuildinfo
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
.next/
.turbo/
.vite/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One rule per pattern in `env.guarded` (harness.config.json): the file the secret guard refuses
# to open and the file git refuses to track are the same list. `harness doctor` probes each and
# prints the missing line when one is absent. To publish the SHAPE of a configuration, commit a
# scaffolding twin (`.example`, `.template`, `.sample`); the guard deliberately does not match
# those, so add a `!` negation for the twin BELOW the rules of this section.
.env
.env.*

# ── Agent runtime: shared settings are tracked, personal ones are not ──
# .claude/settings.json is the hook registration and IS this repo. The local file is one
# person's permissions and may hold a credential in its env block.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Safety copies taken while changing the tracked settings (settings.json.<suffix>). Kept on disk
# on purpose, since they hold intermediate states that are in no commit, and never versioned.
.claude/settings.json.*
!.claude/settings.json

# ── Commit-hygiene waiver (local, per tree state) ─────────────────
# Written by `commit-hygiene.cjs --clear` to waive a deliberate finding. Bound to a hash of the
# tree it was granted for, so it is worthless to anyone else and dies on the next change.
.claude/.commit-hygiene-clearance.json

# ── Gate run output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# gates.json is the verdict of ONE run on ONE machine: it carries a timestamp, a node version
# and a dirty flag, so versioning it would put a conflict in every pull and a figure in the diff
# of every branch. Its COMMITTED counterpart, gates.baseline.json, is the agreed figure and is
# deliberately NOT ignored — moving that one is a deliberate re-baseline whose commit subject
# must start `gates:` (scripts/harness/guards/commit-hygiene.cjs).
scripts/harness/gates.json
# A red gate's whole output, one file per gate, kept beside it by gates.js. `*.log` above
# already covers it; named here so removing that rule cannot put a gate's output in a commit.
scripts/harness/gates.red.*.log

# ── Stray shell brace-expansion leftovers ─────────────────────────
# A mis-quoted brace command can drop a literal file named "{," or "{,bak}" into the tree.
{,*
{,}
